From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the comparison type of an ART scan predicate

ART::TryInitializeScan() declares the comparison type of each conjunct
without a value and has TryMatchComparison() fill it in. Every path that
returns true assigns it, but GCC 13 at -O2 cannot see that through the
matcher and reports -Wmaybe-uninitialized where IsLowerBound() reads it.
Starting it at ExpressionType::INVALID changes nothing at run time.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/execution/index/art/art.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/execution/index/art/art.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/execution/index/art/art.cpp
index adb87de0da..5bde3c187e 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/execution/index/art/art.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/execution/index/art/art.cpp
@@ -298,7 +298,7 @@ unique_ptr<IndexScanState> ART::TryInitializeScan(const Expression &expr, const
 			return nullptr;
 		}
 		for (auto &comparison : comparisons) {
-			ExpressionType comparison_type;
+			ExpressionType comparison_type = ExpressionType::INVALID;
 			Value constant_value;
 			if (!TryMatchComparison(expr, comparison.get(), comparison_type, constant_value)) {
 				return nullptr;
